  "question": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{10}^{19} \\frac{\\sin x}{1+x^{6}} d x$. Then,"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$|I|    < 10^{-9}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$|I|    < 10^{-7}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$|I|    < 10^{-5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$|I|>10^{-7}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $x>10,$ we have\r\n$|\\sin x|    < 1$ and $1+x^{8}>10^{8}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{1}{1+x^{8}} \\leq 10^{-8}$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad\\left|\\int_{10}^{19} \\frac{\\sin x}{1+x^{8}} d x\\right| \\leq \\int_{10}^{19} \\frac{|\\sin x|}{1+x^{8}} d x$\r\n$\\quad \\leq \\int_{10}^{19} 10^{-8}=9 \\times 10^{-8} < 10^{-7}$"
  }
}